.TH HV_VSS_DAEMON 8 2026-09-21 "Linux 7.0.9" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
hv_vss_daemon \- Hyper-V guest online backup (VSS) daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hv_vss_daemon
.RB [ \-n ]
.br
.B hv_vss_daemon
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hv_vss_daemon
is the user-space side of the Hyper-V online backup (VSS) service in a
Linux guest.
When the host takes a snapshot of the running guest, it asks the guest
to freeze its file systems first and to thaw them afterwards.
The kernel's Hyper-V utilities driver passes these requests to the
daemon through the character device
.IR \%/dev/\:vmbus/\:hv_vss ;
the daemon carries out each request and writes the result back to the
device.
.PP
At startup the daemon detaches from the terminal with
.BR daemon (3)
unless
.B \-n
is given; the working directory is not changed, and standard input,
standard output and standard error are redirected to
.IR /dev/null .
It then opens the device, registers with the kernel, reads the version
that the kernel driver reports, and serves requests until it is killed.
If a read from or a write to the device fails, for example across
hibernation, the daemon closes the device, thaws any file systems it
has frozen, reopens the device and registers again.
It exits if the thaw fails.
.SS Freeze and thaw
On a freeze request, the daemon reads
.I /proc/mounts
and freezes, with the
.B FIFREEZE
.BR ioctl (2)
on the mount point, every mounted file system whose source is a path
beginning with
.IR /dev/ ,
except:
.IP \(bu 3
file systems mounted read-only;
.IP \(bu 3
file systems of type
.BR vfat ;
.IP \(bu 3
file systems on a loop device, or on a device built on top of a loop
device, as determined from the
.I loop
and
.I slaves
entries under
.IR \%/sys/\:dev/\:block/ major : minor .
.PP
The root file system, if it qualifies, is frozen last.
The daemon ignores
.B EBUSY
from
.BR FIFREEZE ,
which is the error returned when a file system that is mounted more
than once is frozen a second time.
If any other freeze fails, the daemon thaws every file system it
selected and reports the failure to the host.
.PP
On a thaw request, the daemon thaws the same set of file systems with
the
.B FITHAW
.BR ioctl (2),
ignoring
.B EINVAL
from a file system that is already thawed.
A failed thaw is also reported to the host.
.PP
The daemon also answers the host's check for hot backup support, which
it always reports as successful.
Any other request is logged as illegal and answered with success.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-daemon
Stay in the foreground; do not detach from the terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary to standard error and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B hv_vss_daemon
exits with status 0 after
.BR \-\-help ,
and with status 1 for an invalid option, if
.BR daemon (3)
fails, or on a fatal error such as failing to open
.IR \%/dev/\:vmbus/\:hv_vss ,
failing to register with the kernel, or failing to thaw file systems
before reopening the device.
When the daemon detaches, the invoking process exits with status 0 as
soon as the background process has been created; later errors are
reported only in the system log.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I \%/dev/\:vmbus/\:hv_vss
VSS device, provided by the kernel's Hyper-V utilities driver.
.TP
.I /proc/mounts
List of mounted file systems to freeze and thaw.
.TP
.IR \%/sys/\:dev/\:block/ major : minor /
Used to detect file systems on loop devices.
.SH NOTES
The daemon logs through
.BR syslog (3)
with the identifier
.RB \(dq "Hyper\-V VSS" \(dq
and the facility
.BR \%LOG_USER .
.PP
The daemon works only in a Linux guest running on Hyper-V.
.I \%/dev/\:vmbus/\:hv_vss
is created by the kernel's Hyper-V utilities driver, hv_utils
.RB \%( CONFIG_HYPERV_UTILS );
if the device cannot be opened, the daemon exits.
.PP
A freeze request fails as a whole if any selected file system cannot be
frozen, for example because its type does not support freezing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR \%hv_fcopy_uio_daemon (8),
.BR \%hv_kvp_daemon (8),
.BR lsvmbus (1),
.BR ioctl (2),
.BR daemon (3),
.BR syslog (3)
.PP
.I \%Documentation/\:virt/\:hyperv/
in the Linux source.
